From: Omarchy J716s bringup
Subject: [PATCH] accel/ane: admit pinned 27.3 geometry and bound IPC to its request

Base: 8ab10100a4c1c944797e3fc8345589aff57777df
Apply after kernel-j716s-media-handoff-diagnostics.patch. The prepared kernel
source is never edited; this patch targets that immutable base plus diagnostics.

Port the geometry/build table and larger IPC request from upstream PR #1746:
https://github.com/aurora-silicon/linux/pull/1746
Its reviewed J714s iBoot TEXT pin is the only new admission pin. The retained
J716s IM4P TEXT fca6a59af20e3964067d300ec75c8c1bf88bfdaf55b37d2e34808dd1b725b90d
is NOT a live preload pin and is not admitted. J716s live TEXT remains unmeasured.
The two layouts both end at DVA 0x1000036c000; no DATA patchbay is invented.

Fix the review boundary: allocate the 0x14000-byte page-aligned IPC capacity,
then pass only the requested bytes to the actual transport/parser and init
record. Reject truncated/unaligned tables, overlapping/out-of-range rings,
overflowing/un-aligned/overlapping preload ranges, and mixed-build layouts.
The selected TEXT pin stays fixed across metadata rereads, copies and restarts.

Refusal diagnostics read TEXT only from a recognized exact-size layout with
both enabled, nonreusable no-map reservations outside System RAM and the ANE
identity. A digest mismatch is logged, not enrolled. Existing raw-loader,
kexec/kdump, PMGR/PWGATE/DART and lifetime/ownership checks remain mandatory.
For a first safe live-pin observation use the boot-only/read-only option
ane_t6021.ane_observe_only=1: even a verified loader handoff then refuses
acquisition before observer MMIO mapping, power, DMA or engine access. This
option adds no writable loader marker, memory reader or pin override.

This source candidate is not built, installed, booted or hardware-qualified.
Host regressions: scripts/test-ane-27_3.py --kernel FRESH_PATCHED_SOURCE
---
diff --git a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_fw_platform.h b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_fw_platform.h
--- a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_fw_platform.h
